#### 3. `OF:549` — `of_add_device`
* **1. REACH:** **UNREACHABLE** from guest execution (and unreachable during machine init).[cite: 1]
  * **Reason from code:** `of_add_device` (`OF:534`) is `static` to `of.c` and is called only from `of_emul_init` (`OF:969`, `OF:980`–`OF:982`, `OF:1013`, `OF:1017`, `OF:1027`, `OF:1032`, `OF:1037`), `of_emul_init_isa` (`OF:734`), `of_emul_init_adb` (`OF:762`), `of_emul_init_zs` (`OF:794`, `OF:809`, `OF:829`), and `of_emul_init_uninorth` (`OF:859`, `OF:897`, `OF:907`, `OF:908`, `OF:915`).[cite: 1] None of the runtime `OF_SERVICE` callbacks or `of_emul` call `of_add_device`.[cite: 1] Furthermore, during `macppc` init (`MP:99`–`MP:105`), `of_emul_init` first adds `""` with `parentname = ""` (`OF:969`, where `find_device_handle` returns `0` at `OF:118`–`OF:119`, creating handle `1`), and every subsequent call in `MP:99`–`MP:105` passes a `parentname` (`"/"`, `"/io"`, `"/cpus"`, `"/bandit"`, `"/bandit/gc"`, `"/bandit/gc/zs"`) that was already registered immediately prior.[cite: 1] Thus `od->parent < 0` (`OF:546`) is never true.[cite: 1]
* **2. OPTION-SET MEMBER:** None (not guest-reachable; no edit licensed under `R:O4`).[cite: 1]
* **3. DETECTOR:** None (`R:O4`, `R:O5`).[cite: 1]

---

#### 4. `OF:577` — `of_add_prop`
* **1. REACH:** **UNREACHABLE** from guest execution (and unreachable during machine init).[cite: 1]
  * **Reason from code:** `of_add_prop` (`OF:564`) is `static` to `of.c`, called only by `of_add_prop_int32` (`OF:704`), `of_add_prop_str` (`OF:721`), and the `of_emul_init*` functions (`OF:747`, `OF:768`, `OF:778`, `OF:803`, `OF:814`, `OF:822`, `OF:834`, `OF:842`, `OF:873`, `OF:877`, `OF:894`, `OF:901`, `OF:909`, `OF:925`, `OF:935`, `OF:974`, `OF:978`, `OF:1006`, `OF:1030`, `OF:1045`, `OF:1046`).[cite: 1] Every `devname` passed in `of_emul_init*` is registered via `of_add_device` before `of_add_prop*` is called on it.[cite: 1] No `OF_SERVICE` or runtime path calls `of_add_prop`.[cite: 1]
* **2. OPTION-SET MEMBER:** None (not guest-reachable; no edit licensed under `R:O4`).[cite: 1]
* **3. DETECTOR:** None (`R:O4`, `R:O5`).[cite: 1]

---

#### 5. `OF:1100` — `of_emul` (`if (of_data == NULL)`) (`ofemulnodata`)
* **1. REACH:**
  * **Machines:**
    * **ARM:** Every ARM machine (since `MP` `machine_macppc.c` is the only caller of `of_emul_init` at `MP:99`, `machine->md.of_data` is `NULL` on all ARM machines).[cite: 1]
    * **PowerPC:** Every non-`macppc` PowerPC machine, AND `macppc` when `!machine->prom_emulation` (`MP:93`–`MP:94` returns before `MP:99` `of_emul_init`).[cite: 1]
  * **Instruction sequence & privilege:**
    * **ARM:** Executing instruction word `0xef8c64be` (`AI:5034`) in **any** privilege mode (user or privileged; `SWI` encoding `case 0xf:` at `AI:5026` has no privilege check, and `0xef8c64be` has condition field `0xe` = `AL`).[cite: 1] Witnessed in `W:8` (`swi 0xef8c64be` at PC `0x00008000` exits 1).[cite: 1]
    * **PowerPC:** Executing instruction word `0x44ee0002` (`PI:4400`) in **any** privilege mode (user or supervisor; `case PPC_HI6_SC:` at `PI:4397` has no privilege check).[cite: 1]
* **2. OPTION-SET MEMBER (`R:O1`, `R:O2`) & CALLER TAIL (`R:O6`):**
  * **Choice:** `5 FAULT` — deliver the architectural exception that the instruction word natively encodes (`cond_instr(swi)` on ARM at `AI:5029`, `instr(sc)` on PowerPC at `PI:4404`) when `cpu->machine->md.of_data == NULL`, **rather than editing inside `of_emul`**.[cite: 1]
  * **Availability check (`R:O2`):**
    * **ARM:** In `AI:5026`–`AI:5038`, `ic->f = cond_instr(swi); ic->arg[0] = addr & 0xfff;` is ALREADY set as the default handler at `AI:5029`–`AI:5030` before the `else if (iword == 0xef8c64be)` override at `AI:5034`![cite: 1] In `0xef8c64be`, bits 31..28 are `0xe` (`AL`, unconditional) and bits 27..24 are `0xf` (`SWI`), so architectural ARM execution of `0xef8c64be` is an unconditional SWI exception (`cond_instr(swi)`).[cite: 1]
    * **PowerPC:** In `PI:4397`–`PI:4405`, `ic->arg[0] = (iword >> 5) & 0x7f; ic->arg[1] = (addr & 0xfff) + 4;` is ALREADY populated at `PI:4398`–`PI:4399` before `if (iword == 0x44ee0002)` at `PI:4400`, with the `else` branch setting `ic->f = instr(sc);` (`PI:4404`), which synchronizes `cpu->pc = (cpu->pc & ~0xfff) + ic->arg[1]` and calls `ppc_exception(cpu, PPC_EXCEPTION_SC)` (`PI:3944`–`PI:3946`).[cite: 1] (Note: whether `0x44ee0002` with reserved bits set triggers `PPC_EXCEPTION_SC` or program check on real hardware is irrelevant to `R:O2` because `PI:4397` already decodes the entire `PPC_HI6_SC` opcode group to `instr(sc)` using `ic->arg[0]` and `ic->arg[1]`.)[cite: 1]
  * **Why a decoder-level gate (or `X(openfirmware)` fallback) beats editing inside `of_emul` (`R:O6` caller-tail trace):**
    * Look at what happens if you instead edit `of_emul` (`OF:1098`) to return early when `of_data == NULL`:
      1. `X(openfirmware)` on ARM (`AI:988`–`AI:996`) calls `of_emul(cpu)` (`AI:991`) **ignoring its return value**, then unconditionally executes:
         ```c
         cpu->pc = cpu->cd.arm.r[ARM_LR];
         if (cpu->machine->show_trace_tree)
             cpu_functioncall_trace_return(cpu);
         quick_pc_to_pointers_arm(cpu);
         ```
         (`AI:992`–`AI:995`).[cite: 1]
      2. `X(openfirmware)` on PowerPC (`PI:3956`–`PI:3966`) likewise calls `of_emul(cpu)` (`PI:3958`) **ignoring its return value**, then unconditionally executes:
         ```c
         cpu->pc = cpu->cd.ppc.spr[SPR_LR];
         if (cpu->machine->show_trace_tree)
             cpu_functioncall_trace_return(cpu);
         quick_pc_to_pointers(cpu);
         ```
         (`PI:3960`–`PI:3964`).[cite: 1]
      3. Therefore, if `of_emul` merely declines and returns when `of_data == NULL`, a user-mode guest executing `0xef8c64be` (ARM) or `0x44ee0002` (PPC) on a machine without OpenFirmware does **not** take a syscall/SWI trap and does **not** advance `pc` to `pc + 4` — instead, it **branches to `LR`** (`r[14]` / `SPR_LR`) as if `swi 0x8c64be` / `sc` were a return-to-link-register instruction (and if `of_emul` reaches `OF:1193`–`OF:1199`, it also clobbers `r[0]` or `gpr[3]`)![cite: 1]
    * By contrast, gating in the decoders:
      * **ARM (`AI:5034`):** `else if (iword == 0xef8c64be && cpu->machine->md.of_data != NULL)` leaves `ic->f = cond_instr(swi)` (`AI:5029`) in place when `of_data == NULL`.[cite: 1]
      * **PowerPC (`PI:4400`):** `if (iword == 0x44ee0002 && cpu->machine->md.of_data != NULL)` takes the `else` branch `ic->f = instr(sc)` (`PI:4404`) when `of_data == NULL`.[cite: 1]
      * *(Check on initialization order:* `of_emul_init` sets `machine->md.of_data = ofd` at `OF:1078` during `machine_macppc` setup at `MP:99`, before any guest instruction page is translated by the dyntrans decoder. Even if `of_data` could ever be NULL in `X(openfirmware)`, keeping `if (of_data == NULL) return 0;` in `OF:1098` or gating in `X(openfirmware)` is harmless, but gating at `AI:5034` and `PI:4400` directly uses the already-prepared `ic->arg` fields for `cond_instr(swi)` and `instr(sc)` without touching `X(swi)`.)[cite: 1]
* **3. WHAT A DETECTOR MUST PIN (`R:O7`):**
  * **Fault/exception row on ARM (no `of_data`):** Executing `0xef8c64be` on an ARM machine does not exit the emulator and does NOT jump to `LR`; it takes the ARM SWI exception vector (`0x00000008`, saving return address in `lr_svc` and switching to SVC mode, matching an ordinary `swi` instruction).[cite: 1]
  * **Fault/exception row on PowerPC without OpenFirmware (e.g. non-`macppc` PPC machine, or `macppc` without `prom_emulation`):** Executing `0x44ee0002` does not exit the emulator and does NOT jump to `SPR_LR`; it delivers `PPC_EXCEPTION_SC` (`SRR0 = pc + 4`, jumping to the SC vector `0x00000c00` / `0xfff00c00`, matching an ordinary `sc` instruction).[cite: 1]
  * **Accept row on `macppc` with `prom_emulation` (`R:O7`):** Executing `0x44ee0002` on `macppc` (where `machine->md.of_data != NULL`) still dispatches to `X(openfirmware)` -> `of_emul(cpu)`, executes the requested OF service (e.g. `"finddevice"` `"/"` returning handle `1` in `base + 16` and `0` in `gpr[3]`), and sets `pc = SPR_LR`.[cite: 1]

---

#### 6. `OF:1120` — `of_emul` (`switch (cpu->cpu_family->arch)` entry `default:`)
* **1. REACH:** **UNREACHABLE**.[cite: 1]
  * **Reason from code:** `of_emul` has only two callers in the codebase (`L:62`): `X(openfirmware)` in `cpu_arm_instr.c` (`AI:991`, where `cpu->cpu_family->arch == ARCH_ARM`, handled at `OF:1113`) and `X(openfirmware)` in `cpu_ppc_instr.c` (`PI:3958`, where `cpu->cpu_family->arch == ARCH_PPC`, handled at `OF:1116`).[cite: 1] Moreover, only `machine_macppc.c` (`MP:99`, `ARCH_PPC`) initializes `of_data` (`OF:1078`), so no other architecture can ever reach `OF:1112`.[cite: 1]
* **2. OPTION-SET MEMBER:** None (unreachable; `R:O4`).[cite: 1]
* **3. DETECTOR:** None (`R:O4`, `R:O5`).[cite: 1]

---

#### 7. `OF:1201` — `of_emul` (`switch (cpu->cpu_family->arch)` exit `default:`)
* **1. REACH:** **UNREACHABLE**.[cite: 1]
  * **Reason from code:** Identical `switch (cpu->cpu_family->arch)` on `ARCH_ARM` (`OF:1194`) and `ARCH_PPC` (`OF:1197`) as `OF:1112`–`OF:1121` in the same function `of_emul`, with no intervening modification to `cpu->cpu_family->arch`.[cite: 1] Any execution reaching `OF:1193` already matched `ARCH_ARM` or `ARCH_PPC` at `OF:1112`–`OF:1118`.[cite: 1]
* **2. OPTION-SET MEMBER:** None (unreachable; `R:O4`).[cite: 1]
* **3. DETECTOR:** None (`R:O4`, `R:O5`).[cite: 1]

